ays old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent David Rouzer (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 7th District leans Republican by about seven points, and David Rouzer seeks another term with the advantages that usually decide such races: incumbency, name recognition, and a dominant war chest. He has raised roughly $2.5 million and holds about $2.1 million on hand, while Democrat Kimberly Hardy has raised under $400,000 and had about $20,000 available in the most recent filings. A Libertarian, Maad Abu-Ghazalah, also appears on the ballot but has run a minimal campaign.\n\nRatings from ten outlets range from Likely to Safe Republican, and the only public poll, conducted by a Democratic-leaning firm in August, showed Rouzer ahead by six. Prediction markets are somewhat more optimistic about Hardy than the raters are, reflecting the Democratic-tilted national environment, but her financial position leaves little margin for error. Rouzer's absence from a candidate forum drew local notice but has not altered the race's fundamentals.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0898, "margin": -8.11}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0938, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0915, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1198, "margin": -8.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0905, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0876, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0761, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0866, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1136, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1231, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.075, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1106, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1174, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.058, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "202